      "text": "My Lord is exalted (sometimes abbreviated into Adoram). The officer “over the levy” who superintended the forced labor employed in public works during the reigns of David, Solomon, and Rehoboam (2 Sam. 20:24; 1 Kgs. 4:6; 5:14; 12:18); death of, by stoning (2 Chr. 10:18, where he is called Hadoram).",
